,ĠifĠmyĠparentsĠcontrolĠwhatĠIĠwatchĠorĠaccess,ĠthatĠmightĠlimitĠmyĠexposureĠtoĠdiverseĠperspectives.ĊĊAnotherĠthought:ĠmaybeĠit'sĠaboutĠtheĠbalanceĠbetweenĠguidanceĠandĠautonomy.ĠAsĠIĠgrowĠolder,ĠIĠshouldĠhaveĠmoreĠsayĠinĠwhatĠIĠdoĠandĠthink.ĠButĠhowĠdoesĠthatĠtransitionĠhappen?ĠIsĠitĠsomethingĠthatĠjustĠhappensĠnaturallyĠasĠIĠgetĠolder,ĠorĠdoĠIĠneedĠtoĠactivelyĠseekĠmoreĠindependence?ĊĊIĠalsoĠwonderĠifĠthereĠareĠstudiesĠorĠresearchĠonĠhowĠparentalĠinfluenceĠaffectsĠmoralĠdevelopment.ĠIĠthinkĠIĠrememberĠsomethingĠaboutĠauthoritativeĠparentingĠstylesĠbeingĠbeneficial,ĠbutĠI'mĠnotĠsureĠhowĠthatĠtiesĠintoĠmoralĠjudgmentĠspecifically.ĊĊInĠsummary,ĠI'mĠtryingĠtoĠunderstandĠifĠbeingĠaĠteenagerĠwithĠparentsĠmakingĠmostĠdecisionsĠaffectsĠhowĠIĠformĠmyĠownĠmoralĠjudgment.ĠItĠseemsĠlikeĠit'sĠaĠmixĠofĠinfluenceĠfromĠparents,Ġpeers,Ġeducation,ĠandĠpersonalĠexperiences.ĠButĠI'mĠnotĠentirelyĠclearĠonĠhowĠallĠtheseĠfactorsĠinteractĠandĠwhetherĠI'mĠtrulyĠdevelopingĠmyĠownĠbeliefsĠorĠjustĠreflectingĠwhatĠothersĠtellĠme.ĊĊIĠguessĠIĠneedĠtoĠlookĠintoĠtheoriesĠofĠmoralĠdevelopment,ĠmaybeĠsomethingĠbyĠLawrenceĠKohlbergĠorĠCarolĠGilligan.ĠKohlbergĠtalkedĠaboutĠstagesĠofĠmoralĠreasoning,ĠsoĠmaybeĠbeingĠinĠaĠstageĠwhereĠothersĠshapeĠmyĠthinkingĠisĠaĠnaturalĠpartĠofĠthatĠprocess.ĠButĠhowĠdoesĠthatĠtransitionĠtoĠmakingĠmyĠownĠjudgments?ĊĊAlso,ĠIĠshouldĠconsiderĠtheĠconceptĠofĠautonomy.ĠAsĠIĠgrowĠolder,ĠIĠshouldĠbeĠableĠtoĠmakeĠmoreĠdecisionsĠonĠmyĠown,ĠwhichĠwouldĠhelpĠmeĠformĠmyĠownĠmoralĠjudgment.ĠButĠhowĠmuchĠcontrolĠdoĠIĠhaveĠinĠthatĠprocess?ĠIsĠitĠsomethingĠIĠhaveĠtoĠactivelyĠworkĠtowards,ĠorĠdoesĠitĠhappenĠasĠIĠmature?ĊĊIĠthinkĠIĠneedĠtoĠbreakĠthisĠdownĠintoĠsmallerĠparts.ĠFirst,ĠunderstandingĠwhatĠmoralĠjudgmentĠis.ĠThen,ĠlookingĠatĠhowĠdifferentĠinfluencesĠ(parents,Ġpeers,Ġeducation)ĠshapeĠit.ĠFinally,ĠfiguringĠoutĠhowĠIĠcanĠdevelopĠmyĠownĠjudgmentĠdespiteĠtheseĠinfluences.ĊĊMaybeĠIĠcanĠstartĠbyĠreflectingĠonĠmyĠownĠexperiences.ĠHaveĠthereĠbeenĠtimesĠwhenĠIĠmadeĠaĠdecisionĠthatĠwasĠdifferentĠfromĠwhatĠmyĠparentsĠwanted?ĠHowĠdidĠthatĠfeel?ĠDidĠIĠfeelĠconfidentĠinĠmyĠchoice,ĠorĠwasĠIĠunsure?ĊĊIĠalsoĠthinkĠaboutĠtheĠimportanceĠofĠcriticalĠthinking.ĠIfĠIĠcanĠanalyzeĠdifferentĠviewpointsĠandĠdecideĠwhatĠmakesĠsenseĠtoĠme,ĠthatĠmightĠhelpĠinĠformingĠmyĠownĠmoralĠjudgment.ĠButĠhowĠdoĠIĠdevelopĠthatĠskillĠifĠmostĠofĠmyĠinformationĠcomesĠfromĠmyĠparentsĠorĠschool?ĊĊPerhapsĠtalkingĠtoĠothersĠmyĠageĠwouldĠhelp.ĠDoĠtheyĠfeelĠtheĠsameĠwayĠaboutĠtheirĠparentsĠmakingĠdecisions?ĠHowĠdoĠtheyĠapproachĠformingĠtheirĠownĠbeliefs?ĠMaybeĠthereĠareĠstrategiesĠorĠapproachesĠIĠcanĠlearnĠfromĠthem.ĊĊInĠconclusion,ĠbeingĠaĠteenagerĠwithĠparentsĠmakingĠmostĠdecisionsĠdoesĠinfluenceĠhowĠIĠformĠmyĠmoralĠjudgment,ĠbutĠit'sĠnotĠtheĠonlyĠfactor.ĠIt'sĠaĠcombinationĠofĠvariousĠinfluences,ĠandĠasĠIĠgrowĠolder,ĠIĠcanĠtakeĠmoreĠcontrolĠoverĠshapingĠmyĠownĠbeliefs.ĠUnderstandingĠtheĠprocessĠandĠactivelyĠseekingĠopportunitiesĠtoĠmakeĠdecisionsĠmightĠhelpĠinĠdevelopingĠmyĠownĠmoralĠjudgment.Ċ",
